refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;

 stringfalsezlib_get_coding_type



 Returns the coding type used for output compression.

&reftitle.returnvalues;
Possible return values are gzip, deflate, or &false;.
The coding type is only known once output compression has been negotiated: zlib.output_compression is enabled (or ob_gzhandler is used) and the Accept-Encoding header of the request contains gzip or deflate. gzip is returned when both are present. In every other case, such as output compression being off or the client advertising neither encoding, &false; is returned.
